## 1. Progression timeline

Skill points follow the compendium: 1 per level from Lv 2–30 (29) plus 3 per promotion (6) = **35 points total**. After Section 5's tree changes, no class can buy everything.

| Level | Ultimate | Baseline skills | Trees and traits |
|-------|----------|-----------------|------------------|
| 1 | Tier 1 unlocks (Seven Cuts, Ten Count, Scrapfall, Sunfall Cataclysm, Orbital Ion Singularity) | Rank 1 of all 3 baseline skills | Intrinsic trait Rank I |
| 2–14 | none | none | Skill points go to class-tree passives and the first choice nodes. Class tree rows 1–3 open up |
| 15 | Tier 2 (count +1 step) | Rank 2 (count +1 step) | Spec skills 1–2 and their forks, spec trait Rank I, intrinsic Rank II |
| 30 | Tier 3 (transformed; spec-dependent except Sena) and the Awakening Mutation fork (FIELD / BURST) | Rank 3 | Spec skills 3–4 and their forks, spec trait Rank II, intrinsic Rank III, class capstones reachable |
| 45 | Tier 4 (Mastery) | Rank 4 | Spec trait Rank III, intrinsic Rank IV |
| 50 | Level cap | | |

**Design rule:** tiers and skill ranks come free from level, not from skill points. Skill points buy choices (nodes, forks, capstones) on top. This keeps count-based upgrades predictable and makes the 35 points matter for build identity.

**Tier rule (new):** a Tier 3 ult's total must be **at least 1.10× the same class's Tier 2 total**. In the current code, Crane Drop (600%) is 16% *below* Scrapfall at Tier 2 (715%), which this rule forbids.

