**Decision: keep the single ult line with riders** (not three separate Tier 3 ults). Riders cannot add swords or change the zone.

| Spec | Rider at Lv 30 (trait Rank II) | Rider at Lv 45 (trait Rank III) |
|------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| Phantom Edge | Each Echo Anchor / decoy inside the zone attracts 2 of the swords onto its marked enemy (they cannot miss) | A perfect evasion during the rain refunds an Echo Anchor charge |
| Rift Breaker | Faultline Stomp fractures inside the zone double the Bleed duration of swords embedded in them | The Great Sword leaves a secondary seismic fracture that detonates after 1.0s |
| Pulse Dancer | The 3 (or 4) rain waves land on the beat and each builds 1 Harmony | At 5 Harmony the Great Sword chains lightning to up to 3 nearby foes |

### 4.6 Awakening Mutation (spec tree row 6 fork)

It applies to **Tier 3 and Tier 4 forms only (decided)**.

**The forks are now defined by role so they stay even:**
- **FIELD = coverage.** +2 primary count (or +1 for ults with 3 or fewer counts) and +15% radius. The added units are tuned so FIELD's **total damage gain is +8–10%**. If it would be more, reduce the per-unit damage of the whole ult so the pool is shared.
- **BURST = payoff.** +20% payoff damage and **+0.3s stun** (only where the ult has a payoff stun). At 45–62% payoff share this lands at about +9–12% total.
- Fork bonuses count toward the Section 2.1 caps.

Why: with the original numbers FIELD was worth +33–50% of the counted portion of damage and BURST about +9–12% of the total, so FIELD was roughly 2–3× stronger.

