### 10.3 Hard rules

1. **No two classes share an impact-frame kind or an accent color.** `signal` belongs to Sena. Rook's Blackout Cascade becomes brass and white-hot, Kaelen's Whiteout Rupture gets a frost tint (a new palette entry), and Vespera's Worldstorm Atlas becomes volt and cyan. Perfect Frequency's volt beat becomes bone or blood.
2. **No two ults from different classes may have the same beat map within ±150ms.** A beat map is the list of action times from the start of the cast to the last damage event.
3. **Pull-in belongs to Ines only.** It is a short pulse of at most 85px displacement, never a held pull. Remove `pullInwardPx` from the Rook, Kaelen and Vespera ults.
4. **Not every ult ends on "stun plus crater".** Each class uses its own payoff rider and ground mark from 10.2. Stun stays where the ult has a payoff stun (it feeds boss stagger), but its visual is the class's own.
5. **No shared opener.** Each class has its own wind-up pose (10.2). None of them may use a letterbox, title card, zoom-lock or world freeze. The only exception is the mob freeze on Seven Cuts and Eight Cuts.
6. **Tier scaling is class-specific** (10.5). No uniform "+1 impact frame" for everyone.
7. **Reduce-flashes mode must still tell classes apart.** Use shape and palette tint, not just flash timing. Sena's inversion becomes a bone tint, with a maximum of 3 flashes per second (the existing cap).

